Adds adblock-rust to Chromium's third-party Rust crates.

Generated with `tools/crates/run_gnrt.py vendor` and `gen` after adding
`adblock` to chromium_crates_io/Cargo.toml (default features off, plus
full-regex-handling; single-thread stays off so the engine is Send + Sync).
The new crates' sources and BUILD.gn files are in Rooster's src/ overlay; this
patch holds the changes to files Chromium already has:

- Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock: the adblock dependency and its resolved crates.
- gnrt_config.toml: settings for the new crates (unsafe allowances, license
  locations, removed build scripts), flatbuffers' build-only dependencies
  dropped (rustc_version, semver), and three changes to existing entries:
  * regex leaves the 'test' group, so it can ship (adblock-rust needs it);
  * aho-corasick may use unsafe code (never built by Chromium before, its
    `false` was untested; regex needs it);
  * thiserror's config is split by version, since only v2's build script
    writes private.rs.
- BUILD.gn / README.chromium of regex, aho_corasick, serde, serde_core and
  bitflags: what gnrt regenerates from the above (no longer testonly, shipped,
  serde's `rc` feature, bitflags' `serde` feature).

